### Integrated stall/recovery history

The current integrated scenario has three recorded passing end-to-end reports (at run IDs `2026-10-25T02-34-28-866Z-37901`, `2026-10-25T02-54-30-363Z-40010`, and `2026-10-25T02-57-32-366Z-40955`). In the newest acceptance invocation it passed as command 3/9. Each passing report confirms real recognition succeeded before the injected next-call hang, the 15-second watchdog expired, underlying worker-thread termination was confirmed, the supervised child closed, and a new child recovered the reported screenshot exactly. Earlier timeouts and an older harness report that used a stale script path and failed on `started is not defined` are retained as historical evidence; they are not deleted or reclassified as passes. This establishes repeatable current passes, but Windows target-runtime behavior still needs validation.

