## 6. Sequential reliability, timeout and cleanup

- The launcher's current integrated sequence intentionally completes one real recognition pass, injects a hang on the following `recognize()`, requires `OCR_OPERATION_TIMEOUT`, requires confirmed underlying worker termination and confirmed failed-child closure, then launches a fresh child to OCR the reported real screenshot. The newest acceptance run passed this end-to-end scenario.
- All three five-image sequences and both two-image order checks were run in subprocesses with the network guard propagated using `NODE_OPTIONS`. Their child logs show close events and the sequence reports show exact matches and complete required fields.
- `testdata/phase1-evidence/acceptance-blocked-network-attempts.log` is empty; the acceptance JSON independently records `blockedAttemptsDetected: false`.
- Earlier transient attempts and the stale-harness `started is not defined` report remain preserved for audit; the latest acceptance launcher does not use that old script path.

## 7. Native vs. Tesseract.js comparison

The JavaScript fallback has current exact-match evidence described above. Native Tesseract 5.5.0 ran on the Linux host and its direct PSM 3 text outputs are retained. A separate `OCR_ENGINE=auto` native pipeline diagnostic matched only 1/4 fixture records exactly, so it is diagnostic evidence, not acceptance. The native engine comparison requested for Windows remains blocked until the Windows CLI path is located/installed and its results are saved separately. Do not substitute a Linux native diagnostic for that gate.

## 8. Correction-data / feedback system

No Phase 6 user-correction-linked diagnostic collection system is included in this closeout. Current `testdata/phase1-evidence` files are test artifacts, not a production feedback database. No automatic OCR learning from unverified output was introduced. A future Phase 6 implementation must keep collection local by default, make retention and deletion explicit, enforce quotas/rotation/deduplication, avoid credential collection, and mark ground truth only after user confirmation.

